    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Compile template_config.json through Blueprint XML, apply it, and export MP4.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --config TEXT:FILE REQUIRED \r\n                              Path to the template_config.json source of truth.\r\n          --ref TEXT REQUIRED Fresh draft reference whose workspace does not already exist,\r\n                              e.g. local://template-preview.\r\n          --output TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              New MP4 output path; an existing file is never overwritten.\r\n          --dir TEXT          Optional parent directory for the new draft workspace.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLE\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft template render --config ./template_config.json \\\r\n      --ref local://template-preview --output ./template-preview.mp4\r\n\r\nThe JSON config is the only authored artifact. XML and resource maps are generated internally.\r\nText config slots accept content plus font/font_size/text_color/text_alpha; sticker slots\r\naccept only a vimo:// resource. Omitted fields preserve the source template.\r\nFailures preserve diagnostic artifacts and require a new ref unless the caller explicitly cleans up.\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
